<section class="lang" id="en" lang="en">
<h1>Delete my account</h1>
<p class="meta">Realmshard (beta), on the web and in the Android app</p>

<h2>In the game (immediate)</h2>
<ol>
<li>Open <strong>Options</strong>, <strong>Save</strong> tab.</li>
<li>In the <strong>Account</strong> section, tap <strong>Delete my account</strong>, then confirm twice (three taps in all). If you last signed in more than 15 minutes ago, the game first asks for your password again.</li>
<li>The account is deleted on the server and the device is signed out. The game then offers to also erase this device’s save.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Without access to the game</h2>
<p class="box">Write to <a href="mailto:pikafpv@gmail.com">pikafpv@gmail.com</a> from your account’s e-mail address, giving your player name. The account is deleted within one month at most, and we answer you once it is done. This is also the way for an account whose e-mail was never confirmed (it cannot sign in).</p>

<h2>What is deleted</h2>
<ul>
<li>The account: e-mail address, encrypted password, id.</li>
<li>The profile and player name.</li>
<li>The cloud saves.</li>
<li>The leaderboard rows (Story, Crowns, Daily Challenge, ranked) and ranked games.</li>
<li>The allegiance and contributions to the War of the Realms.</li>
<li>Gifts received, gift codes used and notification subscriptions.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What remains, unlinked from you</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Reports</strong> (bug or name): kept to fix the game, but without your player name, the account id or the screenshot (erased with the account). The text you wrote stays as it is. The copies the team received by e-mail are erased on request.</li>
<li><strong>Purchase rights</strong> (once purchases open): kept for accounting obligations, not linked to the account.</li>
<li><strong>The save on your device</strong>: it stays until you erase it (the game offers to; otherwise Options › Save › Delete save).</li>
</ul>

